		{"id":"42665d04631a89fb","type":"text","text":"Layer Options:\nButtons and sliders and stuff","x":-370,"y":-80,"width":210,"height":180},
		{"id":"66f989c4155f8b2a","type":"text","text":"the side windows should be dockspaces, containing windows that can be resized, and reorganized","x":-740,"y":-130,"width":340,"height":110},
		{
			"id":"008899175a785fdf",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"It should be possible to hide and unhide these specific side windows, and save the layout to be automatically reloaded on start",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-545,
			"y":-610,
			"width":260,
			"height":150
		},
		{
			"id":"a7e7dcc88790c0db",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"should be possible to add floating buttons to the top side of the editor window",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":10,
			"y":-560,
			"width":260,
			"height":100
		},
		{
			"id":"61830ab0d4f1a440",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"the middle of the screen should be empty, it's where the actual level is shown",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-170,
			"y":360,
			"width":260,
			"height":120
		},
		{
			"id":"31f337bb3e763899",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"i'll load the resource tree to get folders and the sprites/objects, possibly as a struct or big array. I need to be able to go through that as folders and items.\n\nAnd be able to drag in an item into the editor window (to place an instance or a sprite in an asset layer)",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":820,
			"y":-200,
			"width":280,
			"height":300
		}
	],
